{
  "about": "The humanoid alias table: the 22 bones a humanoid rig must have (Godot SkeletonProfileHumanoid names, in profile order) and, per rig family, the joint names to try for each bone, first match wins; a joint matches by its exact name, then by the part after its last ':' or '|' ignoring ASCII case, and a joint an earlier bone took is skipped. A rig takes the family that maps the most bones, ties to the earlier family. genex-anim's humanoid.rs is the runtime copy and its tests/blend.rs holds the two equal; the host's character facts read this file.",
